---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { site, divisions } from '../data/site';
import { verticalsIn, notation } from '../data/verticals';
---
<Base title="About us" description={`${site.name} operates under ${site.parent}, across two divisions and a growing set of business lines.`}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href={url('/')}>Home</a><span>›</span>About</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>A group built on tie-ups</h1>
      <p class="hero__lead">
        {site.name} operates under {site.parent}, across two divisions and a
        growing set of business lines, on one principle: we advise honestly and
        hand you to the partners who deliver.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="gap:3rem;align-items:start">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
          <h2>Why the group is structured this way</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose stack">
          <p>
            Career Plus began in {site.founded} as a coaching institute in Delhi,
            and was registered as {site.parent} with the {site.story.registrar} in
            {site.story.registered}. The purpose then is the purpose now: put
            serious civil services preparation within reach of students who cannot
            buy their way to it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The society was the first in India to teach IAS and PCS subjects the
            industry had passed over, among them mathematics, chemistry,
            agriculture, botany, zoology, statistics, economics, commerce and
            several literatures, and the first to open coaching for the Indian
            Engineering Services and the Indian Forest Services.
          </p>
          <p>
            The group came later, and for a specific reason. Career Plus is a
            service organisation, and the social work it does is paid for by what
            the group earns. Realty &amp; Fin-Serve and Hospitality &amp; Services
            widen that base, and they are held to the same standard as the
            classroom: transparent terms, ethical dealing, and advice that still
            holds up when the customer goes and checks it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Structure</p>
        <h2>How the group is organised</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        {Object.values(divisions).map((d) => (
          <div class="card" data-division={d.id}>
            <div class="card__head">
              <h3 style="margin:0">{d.shortName}</h3>
              <span class="notation">{d.code}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card__body">{d.intro}</p>
            <ul class="trust__list" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
              {verticalsIn(d.id).map((v) => (
                <li><a href={url(`/${v.slug}`)}>{v.name}</a>: <span style="color:var(--ink-soft)">{v.navBlurb}</span></li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="gap:3rem;align-items:start">
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow">Leadership</p>
          <h2>Who runs it</h2>
          <figure class="portrait">
            <img
              src={url(site.leadership.photo)}
              alt={site.leadership.photoAlt}
              width="500"
              height="518"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption>{site.leadership.photoAlt}</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <ul class="people">
            {site.leadership.people.map((person) => (
              <li>
                <strong>{person.name}</strong>
                <span>{person.title}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="prose stack">
          {site.leadership.people.map((person) => (
            <div class="stack leader">
              <h3>{person.name}</h3>
              {person.bio.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
              {person.societyAwards && (
                <p>
                  His work has been recognised with
                  {site.story.awards.map((a, i, all) => (
                    <span>{i === 0 ? ' ' : i === all.length - 1 ? ' and ' : ', '}{a.article}{' '}<strong>{a.name}</strong> in {a.year}</span>
                  ))}, the first awarded by the International Confederation of NGOs.
                </p>
              )}
            </div>
          ))}
          <p>
            The same people who built the classroom operation run the group. That
            is the point of the structure: a family that has answered to students
            and their parents for three decades now answers to buyers, borrowers
            and hotel procurement teams on the same terms.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="gap:3rem;align-items:start">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What we hold to</p>
          <h2>How we behave</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="trust__list">
          <li>We tell you what we are: an intermediary. Our partners lend, build and operate; we know which of them to put you in front of.</li>
          <li>Fees and commissions are stated in writing before work begins.</li>
          <li>We flag the risks in a transaction as plainly as the upside.</li>
          <li>Your information is never passed to a partner without your consent.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
